{code,core,types,ui}: camelCase the lofi.job* wire surface end-to-end

Snake_case leaked across the whole job API: function names
(lofi.job_spawn, lofi.job_notify, ...), input args (timeout_ms on
jobWait, interval_ms on jobNotify), and output payloads (exit_code,
log_path, total_bytes, notify_*) — while the surrounding sandboxed
surface is uniformly camelCase (lofi.bash takes timeoutMs, etc.).

After this change every JS-visible name is camelCase:
 - bindings: jobSpawn, jobStatus, jobRead, jobWait, jobKill, jobNotify
 - inputs:   timeoutMs, intervalMs (jobNotify), notifyIntervalMs,
             notify (jobSpawn)
 - outputs:  exitCode, durationMs, timeoutMs, logPath, totalBytes,
             notify, notifyIntervalMs, notifyChanged
The Rust-side names stay snake_case; only the wire surface moves.

Binding-names and args also flow into the published docs and the
system prompt the model reads, so lofi-code/src/docs/api.md and
lofi-core/src/prompts/system.md move to the new spellings.

Spawn now accepts the two knobs it used to silently drop: notify:
false silences the job entirely, and notifyIntervalMs turns on
periodic ticks without needing a follow-up jobNotify call. Passing
the interval implies notify: true.